WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.550
Ceres, the largest.

00:02.216 --> 00:07.936
Ceres is about nine hundred and fifty kilometres across and holds a quarter of the belt's whole mass.

00:08.414 --> 00:11.059
It is round, so it counts as a dwarf planet.

00:11.636 --> 00:20.107
A spacecraft called Dawn reached it in 2015, the first visit to a dwarf planet, and found large deposits of salt in its crust.
